            <ArticleTitle>Cell culture models for study of differentiated adipose cells.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/scrt527</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adipose cells are an important source of mesenchymal stem cells and are important for direct use in research on lipid metabolism and obesity. In addition to use of primary cultures, there is increasing interest in other sources of larger numbers of cells, using approaches including induced pluripotent stem cell differentiation and viral immortalisation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
